c, Teymur Kheirkhabarov @HeirhabarovT, oscd.community","kind":"sigma"},{"id":"882e858a-3233-4ba8-855e-2f3d3575803d","title":"DNS Query Request By QuickAssist.EXE","status":"experimental","level":"low","logsource":{"category":"dns_query","product":"windows"},"data_path":"data/detection-rules/882e858a-3233-4ba8-855e-2f3d3575803d.json","source_url":"https://github.com/anpa1200/sigma/blob/b249e9683190cffdcaf188ccbfb90bf4759844e1/rules/windows/dns_query/dns_query_win_quickassist.yml","author":"Muhammad Faisal (@faisalusuf)","kind":"sigma"},{"id":"b0ce780f-10bd-496d-9067-066d23dc3aa5","title":"HackTool - SharpWSUS/WSUSpendu Execution","status":"test","level":"high","logsource":{"product":"windows","category":"process_creation"},"data_path":"data/detection-rules/b0ce780f-10bd-496d-9067-066d23dc3aa5.json","source_url":"https://github.com/anpa1200/sigma/blob/b249e9683190cffdcaf188ccbfb90bf4759844e1/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_sharpwsus_wsuspendu_execution.yml","author":"@Kostastsale, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)","kind":"sigma"},{"id":"60bfeac3-0d35-4302-8efb-1dd16f715bc6","title":"Suspicious SysAidServer Child","status":"test","level":"medium","logsource":{"category":"process_creation","product":"windows"},"data_path":"data/detection-rules/60bfeac3-0d35-4302-8efb-1dd16f715bc6.json","source_url":"https://github.com/anpa1200/sigma/blob/b249e9683190cffdcaf188ccbfb90bf4759844e1/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_java_sysaidserver_susp_child_process.yml","author":"Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)","kind":"sigma"},{"id":"1012f107-b8f1-4271-af30-5aed2de89b39","title":"Terminal Service Process Spawn","status":"test","level":"high","logsource":{"product":"windows","category":"process_creation"},"data_path":"data/detection-rules/1012f107-b8f1-4271-af30-5aed2de89b39.json","source_url":"https://github.com/anpa1200/sigma/blob/b249e9683190cffdcaf188ccbfb90bf4759844e1/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_svchost_termserv_proc_spawn.yml","author":"Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)","kind":"sigma"}],"atlas_basic":[],"atlas_anomaly":[],"anomaly_types":[],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0118","name":"Exploitation of Remote Services – multi-platform lateral movement detection","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--ee73dd97-cf1a-4220-a7cf-52d864811bb4","relationship_id":"relationship--0730d238-c81d-415c-9db5-bff7368114d6","description":"","analytics":[{"id":"AN0327","name":"Analytic 0327","guidance":"Correlates inbound network access to remote service ports (e.g., SMB/RPC 445/135, RDP 3389, WinRM 5985/5986) with near-time instability in the target service (crash, abnormal restart), suspicious child process creation under the service, and post-access lateral-movement behaviors. The chain indicates likely exploitation rather than normal administration.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","platforms":["Windows"],"tuning":[{"field":"ServicePortSet","description":"List of monitored service ports (default: 445,135,3389,5985,5986,1433,3306)."},{"field":"TimeWindow","description":"Correlation window between inbound access and crash/child-process (default: 10 minutes)."},{"field":"AllowedAdminCIDRs","description":"Known management networks to suppress benign admin traffic."},{"field":"MinConnErrorRate","description":"Percent of failed/aborted connections to treat as anomalous (default: 30%)."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"WinEventLog:System","channel":"EventCode=1000","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0327","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0327","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0327","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0016","component":"Module Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=7","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0327","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"component_id":"DC0035","component":"Process Access","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=10","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0327","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0327","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"Inbound connections to 445, 3389, 5985-5986 with high error/connection-reset rate, followed by new outbound sessions from the same host to internal assets within short interval.","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0327","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0327","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]},{"id":"AN0328","name":"Analytic 0328","guidance":"Links inbound network access to SSHD/SMB/NFS/Databases or custom daemons with subsequent daemon crash/restart, core dump, or spawning of shells/reverse shells from the service context, indicating remote exploitation.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0328","platforms":["Linux"],"tuning":[{"field":"ServiceNames","description":"Linux daemons to watch (sshd, smbd, nfsd, httpd/nginx, mysqld, postgres, redis)."},{"field":"CoreDumpPaths","description":"Paths indicating crash artifacts (/var/crash, /var/lib/systemd/coredump)."},{"field":"ShellSpawnAllowlist","description":"Paths/users allowed to spawn shells from services (default: empty)."},{"field":"TimeWindow","description":"Correlation window (default 10m)."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"linux:syslog","channel":"kernel|systemd messages indicating 'segmentation fault'|'core dumped'|'service terminated unexpectedly' for sshd, smbd, vsftpd, mysqld, httpd, etc.","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0328","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0328","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"execve of /bin/sh,/bin/bash,/usr/bin/curl,/usr/bin/python by service accounts (e.g., apache, mysql, nobody) immediately after inbound network activity.","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0328","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0328","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"Inbound connections to monitored service ports from external or unusual internal sources; rapid follow-on lateral connections from the same host.","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0328","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0328","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]},{"id":"AN0329","name":"Analytic 0329","guidance":"Detects exploitation targeting ESXi/vCenter by correlating attempts to reach known exploitable endpoints (OpenSLP 427, CIM 5989, Hostd/Vpxa HTTPS 443, ESXi SOAP) with vmkernel/hostd crashes, unexpected hostd/vpxa restarts, or new reverse/outbound connections from ESXi host/vCenter to internal assets.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0329","platforms":["ESXi"],"tuning":[{"field":"ESXiServicePorts","description":"427, 443, 902, 5989; modify per version/hardening."},{"field":"MgmtCIDRs","description":"Legit management networks for vCenter/ESXi."},{"field":"RestartKeywords","description":"Crash/restart patterns to match in logs."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"esxi:hostd","channel":"Keywords: 'Backtrace','Signal 11','PANIC','hostd restarted','assert' or 'Service terminated unexpectedly' in /var/log/hostd.log, /var/log/vmkernel.log, /var/log/syslog.log.","platforms":["ESXi"],"analytic_id":"AN0329","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0329","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"Inbound to tcp/427 (OpenSLP), tcp/443 (vSphere APIs), tcp/902, tcp/5989 followed by new unexpected outbound sessions from the ESXi/vCenter host.","platforms":["ESXi"],"analytic_id":"AN0329","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0329","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]},{"id":"AN0330","name":"Analytic 0330","guidance":"Ties inbound access to exposed services (ARD/VNC 5900, SSH 22, ScreenSharing, web services) with process crashes in unified logs and abnormal child processes spawned under those services (e.g., bash, curl) to indicate exploitation.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0330","platforms":["macOS"],"tuning":[{"field":"ServicePortSet","description":"22, 5900, 8080/8443 by default."},{"field":"AllowedAdmins","description":"MDM/jump-host IPs allowed to manage endpoints."},{"field":"TimeWindow","description":"Default: 10 minutes."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"macos:unifiedlog","channel":"process 'crashed'|'EXC_BAD_ACCESS' for sshd, screensharingd, httpd; launchd restarts of these daemons.","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0330","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0330","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"macos:osquery","channel":"parent_name in ('sshd','httpd','screensharingd') spawning shells or scripting runtimes.","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0330","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0330","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"Inbound to 22/5900/8080 and follow-on internal connections.","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0330","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0118#AN0330","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]}]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","tag":"Application Log Content","page":"telemetry/DC0038/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","tag":"File Creation","page":"telemetry/DC0039/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","tag":"Module Load","page":"telemetry/DC0016/","kind":"attack_component"},{"id":"DC0082","nam